0168-b032"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group><name><surname>Bailey</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Scott-Dupree</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><name><surname>Harris</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><name><surname>Tolman</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Harris</surname><given-names>B</given-names></name></person-group><year>2005</year><article-title>Contact and oral toxicity to honey bees <named-content content-type="genus-species">(Apis mellifera)</named-content> of agents registered for use for sweet corn insect control in Ontario, Canada</article-title><source>Apidologie</source><volume>36</volume><fpage>623</fpage><lpage>633</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="pbio-0050168-b033"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group><name><surname>Decourtye</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Lacassie</surname><given-names>E</given-names></name><name><surname>Pham-Delegue</surname><given-names>MH</given-names></name></person-group><year>2003</year><article-title>Learning performances of honeybees (<named-content content-type="genus-species">Apis mellifera</named-content> L) are differentially affected by imidacloprid according to the season</article-title><source>Pest Manag Sci</source><volume>59</volume><fpage>269</fpage><lpage>278</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12639043</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pbio-0050168-b034"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group><name><surname>Decourtye</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Armengaud</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><name><surname>Renou</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Devillers</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Cluzeau</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><year>2004</year><article-title>Imidacloprid impairs memory and brain metabolism in the honeybee (<named-content content-type="genus-sp